[21.09148, "o", "\u001b[1;39m{\r\n  \u001b[0m\u001b[1;34m\"total_checks\"\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m: \u001b[0m\u001b[0;39m25\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m,\r\n  \u001b[0m\u001b[1;34m\"passed_checks\"\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m: \u001b[0m\u001b[0;39m21\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m,\r\n  \u001b[0m\u001b[1;34m\"failed_checks\"\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m: \u001b[0m\u001b[0;39m4\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m,\r\n  \u001b[0m\u001b[1;34m\"functions_analyzed\"\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m: \u001b[0m\u001b[0;39m0\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m,\r\n  \u001b[0m\u001b[1;34m\"avg_complexity\"\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m: \u001b[0m\u001b[0;39m0.0\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m,\r\n  \u001b[0m\u001b[1;34m\"avg_crap\"\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m: \u001b[0m\u001b[0;39m0.0\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m\r\n\u001b[1;39m}\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[22.098467, "o", "\r\n$ cogent explain crap\r\n"]
[23.107689, "o", "  CRAP (Change Risk Anti-Pattern)\r\n  ───────────────────────────────\r\n\r\n  What it measures\r\n    Measures how risky a function is to change. Combines cyclomatic complexity and test coverage. A high-CRAP function is complex AND untested — the most dangerous kind.\r\n\r\n  Threshold\r\n    max_avg = 15.0  (average CRAP score across all functions)\r\n\r\n  How to read the output\r\n    Score 0-30 is good. Above 30 means many complex functions lack tests. Each function gets a CRAP score; the average is compared to the threshold.\r\n\r\n  Quick fixes\r\n    1. Add unit tests for complex functions (coverage drives CRAP down faster than simplification).\r\n    2. Refactor functions with cyclomatic complexity > 10 into smaller helpers.\r\n    3. Focus on the top 5 offenders shown in the output.\r\n\r\n  ℹ See docs/tools/crap.md for deeper explanation and examples.\r\n\r\n"]
